    <%- include('/common/_metaCreate', { meta }) %>
        <!DOCTYPE html>
        <html lang="en">
        <%- include('/common/_headContent', { meta }) %>

            <body class="page-terms-policy" data-page="../jp">
                <%- include('/common/_header', { meta }) %>

                    <ul class="c-breadcrumbs c-wrapper">
                        <li><a href="<%= meta.basePath %><%= ASSET_PATH %><%= meta.lang %>index.html">Top</a></li>
                        <li class="c-breadcrumbs-arrow">▶︎</li>
                        <li>Privacy Policy</li>
                    </ul>
                    <section class="c-terms-policy c-wrapper">
                        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
                        <p>TCROSS Co., Ltd. and TCROSS Communication Co., Ltd. (collectively, the “Company”) establish
                            this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) regarding the handling of user information, including
                            personal information, of users in connection with the various services provided by the
                            Company, including TCROSS NEWS, clinical-related services, event-related services,
                            consulting services, SaaS-based services, and other services provided by the Company
                            (collectively, the “Services”).
                        </p>
                    </section>
                    <section class="c-policy c-wrapper">
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>1. User Information Collected and Methods of Collection</h2>
                            <p>In this Policy, “User Information” means information relating to the identification of
                                users, as well as information generated or accumulated in connection with the use of the
                                Services and collected by the Company.
                            </p>
                            <p><b>（1）Information Provided by Users</b></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Name (including phonetic spelling), gender, and date of birth</li>
                                <li>Email address, company or organization name, department, workplace location, job
                                    title, telephone number, and other contact information</li>
                                <li>Authentication information such as login IDs and passwords required to use the
                                    Services</li>
                                <li>Information provided through contract application forms, questionnaires, interviews,
                                    or similar means</li>
                                <li>Technical materials, experimental data, and attribute information of research
                                    participants (such as age and gender) necessary for conducting commissioned research
                                </li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><b>（2）Information Collected in Connection with Use of the Services</b></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Usage history and records of clinical-related services</li>
                                <li>Event participation registration information, attendance status, and payment
                                    information</li>
                                <li>Information accompanying contracts and work records in consulting services</li>
                                <li>TCROSS NEWS usage logs (access history, operation history, usage time, IP address,
                                    usage environment, etc.)</li>
                                <li>Records of inquiries and communications regarding the Services</li>
                                <li>Access information automatically collected when using the Company’s websites (access
                                    date and time, pages viewed, IP address, device information, cookies, etc.)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>2. Purpose of Use</h2>
                            <p>User Information will be used for the following purposes:</p>
                            <p><b>（1）Provision and Operation of the Services</b></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Registration acceptance, identity verification, performance of contracts, billing,
                                    and payment processing</li>
                                <li>Provision and quality improvement of services in the clinical, event, consulting,
                                    and SaaS-based businesses</li>
                                <li>Account management, security assurance, and analysis of usage status in SaaS-based
                                    services</li>
                                <li>Responding to inquiries and providing user support</li>
                                <li>Addressing acts that violate contracts or policies</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><b>（2）Other Purposes</b></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Creation and analysis of statistical data for service improvement</li>
                                <li>Providing information on events, seminars, study groups, campaigns, and similar
                                    activities</li>
                                <li>Providing information on new services, research activities, and business activities
                                </li>
                                <li>Necessary communications, document delivery, and survey requests related to
                                    contracts and operations</li>
                                <li>Creation, verification, and reporting of research outcomes</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>3. Management of User Information</h2>
                            <p>The Company shall manage User Information accurately and keep it up to date within the
                                scope necessary to achieve the purposes of use. Personal information that is no longer
                                required to be retained will be promptly disposed of or deleted.
                                Data related to SaaS-based services will also be deleted in accordance with the
                                Company’s prescribed methods after user or corporate account withdrawal or termination
                                of contracts.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>4. Security Control Measures</h2>
                            <p>To protect User Information, the Company implements the following security measures:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Security measures to prevent unauthorized access</li>
                                <li>Prohibition of unnecessary duplication or removal of information</li>
                                <li>Encryption of communications using SSL or similar technologies</li>
                                <li>Access control, log monitoring, and periodic security testing in SaaS-based services
                                </li>
                                <li>Periodic internal audits and continuous improvements</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>5. Outsourcing and Provision to Third Parties</h2>
                            <p>The Company may outsource the handling of User Information to contractors as necessary
                                for business operations. In such cases, the Company will exercise appropriate
                                supervision.
                                Except as required by laws and regulations, the Company will not provide personal
                                information to third parties without the prior consent of the user.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>6. Joint Use</h2>
                            <p>The Company may jointly use User Information within the following scope:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Parties to joint use: TCROSS Co., Ltd. and TCROSS Communication Co., Ltd.</li>
                                <li>Purpose of joint use: Within the scope of the purposes set forth in Section 2</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>7. Disclosure, Correction, and Suspension of Use of Personal Information</h2>
                            <p>If a user requests disclosure, correction, deletion, or suspension of use of their
                                personal information, the Company will respond without delay in accordance with
                                applicable laws and regulations. Please note that a prescribed fee may be charged for
                                requests for disclosure.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
                            <p>For inquiries regarding the handling of User Information, please contact:
                                TCROSS Co., Ltd.  Personal Information Inquiry Desk NEOX Shinjuku Building 7F 1-9-1
                                Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo 160-0022, Japan</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>9. Revisions</h2>
                            <p>The Company may revise this Policy in response to amendments to laws and regulations or
                                changes in its business operations. If there are any material changes, the Company will
                                provide notice on its website or through other appropriate means.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <h2>Supplementary Provision</h2>
                            <p>The privacy policy applicable to TCROSS NEWS is separately posted on the TCROSS NEWS
                                website.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="c-policy-section">
                            <p>End</p>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <%- include('/common/_footer', { meta }) %>
